ahead of its start we got a  behind-the-scenes look at apex legends  season 6 boosted  that includes details that haven't been  fully explained in the trailers that  have been released thus far  with season six about to begin let's go  over everything we know  all right so rampart as we suspected  rampart is a defender she specializes in  directional defense deterring enemy  squads from certain locations while  fortifying her squad's position  her tactical ability is similar to  titanfall 2's a-wall called amped cover  rampart can place five on the  battlefield at a time when first place  they're vulnerable and easily destroyed  but after a few seconds they reinforce  themselves and erect a shield  the shield is one way so make sure  you're not placing it backwards  rampart's ultimate ability is in-place  minigun when used rampart puts down  sheila which she her teammates can use  to lay down suppressive fire the gun  becomes more accurate the longer you  hold the trigger  discouraging you from firing in small  bursts the new legend is pretty unique  in that she's the first to have an  ability that makes her specifically  better with a type of weapon in  comparison to her teammates  rampart's passive ability modded loader  allows her to reload lmgs faster and  gives her 50  more ammo per clip with lmgs in terms of  the lstar which  doesn't have a clip rampart is able to  fire the gun for a longer period of time  before it overheats  speaking of lmgs season 6 sees the  devotion rotated back into the normal  loop pool  and it's bringing back both the  turbocharger hop up and extended energy  mags  in its place the r99 is being rotated  into care packages  don't be sad about the r99 leaving the  general loot pool we have a new smg to  take its place the volt is coming to  apex legends in season six  offering a similar fire rate to the  alternator as an energy ammo gun the  volt's bullets don't lose speed in  mid-air and travel a lot further  giving you a mid to long range smg  option it takes a barrel stabilizer  extended energy mag  smg scope and standard stock attachments  just like season 4's heavy metal and  heat sink flat line  and season 5's precision caliber and  attention to detail wingman  rampart is the designer behind the two  legendary weapons skins you can unlock  for completing season 6's battle pass  get to level 100 and level 110 and  you'll unlock new skins for the g7  both shoot out flames when you get a  kill one is a white g7 that fires blue  flames  and the other is a black g7 that fires  orange flames you're not completely  naked when you drop in apex legends  anymore  all players will now drop with what's  essentially a level 0 evo shield  deal damage and will upgrade to the  standard level 1 evo shield but it won't  fill until you pop a shield cell  from there it will upgrade as normal  dealing damage isn't the only way to  upgrade your evoshield anymore  whether it's the one you start with or  when you loot you can now craft stronger  evo shields with season 6  you'll find materials in loot bins as  well as large caches of materials  scattered throughout world's edge like  treasure packs materials don't take up  inventory space and enemies can't loot  them off you  take these materials to brand new  replicator stations and you'll be able  to turn them in for weapons  ammo hop-ups or evil shield levels you  won't always be able to craft the same  items though while some items will  remain permanent fixtures at replicators  for the season some will only be in the  stations for a week  others may only be in a replicator for a  day before rotating out  one of the best things about materials  is that you don't lose them upon death  so if your teammates  manage to revive you and you have a lot  of materials on you you can find a  replicator and secure some decent loot  instead of hoping to find some untouched  bins  there are plenty of new ways to get  around world's edge too new pathways  have been carved into the mountains like  a tunnel that takes you directly from  the dome to the tree  there are also a lot of new geysers to  ride additionally there are new  locations to visit too  a giant rocket launch pad has been built  between the dome and sorting factory and  drill site has been transformed into a  brand new location  the small unnamed village in the valley  between raj voyage and the vault tunnel  that leads the train yard has been  transformed into a major landmark too  the train is gone and in its place you  can now discover abandoned train cars  and the previously empty tunnels  scattered throughout the map these train  cars hide loot and open up world's edge  tunnel system as a worthwhile avenue for  exploring  and moving around the map there's also a  new addition that may prove the saving  grace or doom for certain squads  blast doors now dot world's edge  activate them and they'll close off  entire lanes  providing you with a means of cutting  off a squad on your heels if you're  caught behind a blast door you'll need  to go around or hope you have a  pathfinder or octane and your squad to  go over  depending on how the zone is closing you  could definitely use a blast door to  funnel most squads in a certain  direction  quest mode returns in season 6 but it  drops the short pve hunt missions  instead you just get more story but it's  not simple text logs this time around  with season 6 quest transitions into a  full-on apex legends comic  created by darkhorse season 6's battle  pass will offer over 100 items including  brand new hollow spray rewards we've  already seen one of them  lobo left one as her calling card in one  of the world's edge volts  ahead of her release in season five  season six has plenty of cool looking  epic and legendary skins as well  including a hooded outfit for bloodhound  and a sweet black and green look for  octane  [Music]  and that's everything we know about apex  legend season 6. for now anyway  be sure to check back in on gamespot  we're putting together a rampart legend  guide  will continue to cover apex legends  throughout season 6 boosted  [Music]  you
 

